  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Better inclusion, greater rights: Promoting economic integration of the most disadvantaged groups of the City of Buenos Aires</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In collaboration with the neighborhood council of Villa 21-24 and other partners, Asociacin Civil por la Igualdad y la Justicia (ACIJ) will create a community center where 150 entrepreneurs will develop the skills and receive the support necessary to make their businesses more competitive and facilitate their entry into the formal economy of Buenos Aires. ACIJ will also help residents of this low-income community benefit from full access to social services and inclusion in economic life. The project should reach 1,500 residents of Villa 21-24 directly and another 25,000 indirectly.</narrative>
  </description>
